lly Concealed Hand (4 points)\n- Maintains flexibility for developing Seven Pairs or other patterns\n- I have multiple pairs which is promising for Seven Pairs path\n\nReason:\nI should **Pass** because:\n1. My hand shows potential for Seven Pairs (currently have 4 pairs: W2-W2, B3-B3, B9-B9, F3-F3)\n2. Exposing a meld by Chi would eliminate the possibility of Seven Pairs and Fully Concealed Hand\n3. The hand is still far from a standard 4-melds-1-pair winning pattern, and Chi B8 doesn't significantly advance that goal\n4. Keeping the hand flexible allows me to draw toward either Seven Pairs or develop pungs/chows naturally\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
