st isolated tile with lowest utility.\n\nReason: \nB9 is an isolated terminal tile that doesn't fit into any sequential pattern with my other Dots tiles. By discarding B9, I maintain my strong Dots sequence (B1-B5) which can form multiple chows, keep my F3 pair (seat wind for potential 2 points), and preserve the option for Half Flush (6 points). The four W2 tiles can still be used later if needed, but keeping hand flexibility is more important now.\n\nAnswer: Play B9"}
